    {'para': '**417.** This root also makes a perfect without reduplication (but otherwise regular) which has always the value of a present. The forms of the indic. are: Sing. 1. ⟨veda⟩, 2. ⟨vettha⟩, 3. ⟨veda⟩; du. 1. ⟨vidva⟩, 2. ⟨vidathus⟩, 3. ⟨vidatus⟩; pl. 1. ⟨vidma⟩, 2. ⟨vida⟩, 3. ⟨vidus⟩. The participle is ⟨vidvāṃs⟩, f. ⟨viduṣī⟩ (cf. § 268).'},
